<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96362" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέαρ</span></b> , τό, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέατος</span> [v. sub fin.]; 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῆρ</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
			703.2
		</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
			6
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Archig.
		</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
			Gal.
			12.861
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Thd.
			<u>Bel.</u>
			27
		</span></i>, gen. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῆτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
					176.183
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεῖαρ</span></b> , gen. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στείατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Choerob.
					<u>in Theod.</u>
					1.350
				</span></i>
			 H.:—<i>hard fat, suet</i>, such as ruminating
			animals have, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πιμελή</span> (soft
			fat), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ δὲ στέατος ἔνεικε μέγαν
			τροχόν</span> a large cake of <i>suet</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				21.178
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτε πιμελὴν οὔτε στέαρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>PA</u>
					651a26
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τῶν ἰχθύων ς. πιμελῶδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HA</u>
					520a21
				</span></i>
			, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> any
				<i>animal fat</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τῆς ἄρκτου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Od.</u>
					63
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. δελφίνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					5.4.28
				</span></i>
			; freq. in <i><span class="en">
				LXX
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				<u>Le.</u>
				3.15
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				16
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				17
			</span></i>, al.); also <i><span class="en">
				<u>PRev.Laws</u>
				50.14
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <u>PCair.Zen.</u> Il.cc.; so
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. χήνειον, ὀρνίθειον</span>, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.76
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταῖς</span>
			 (q.v.), <i>dough made from flour of spelt</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Nat.Mul.</u>
				27
			</span></i> (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταῖς</span> is prob. l.),
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				879a10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.20.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ps.</u>
				80(81).17
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				17.2.5
			</span></i> (citing <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.36
			</span></i>, where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταῖς</span> is in our
			text). [Gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέατος</span> disyll., <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέᾱτι</span> trisyll.,
				<i><span class="en">
				Diph.
				119
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεάτιον</span>.] (Prob. fr.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στᾱ</span><i>y</i><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αρ</span>, cf. Skt. <i>styāyate</i>
			'congeal, grow hard'.)</div>
